 36   c  ABST$Nuclear spectroscopic information for experimentally investigated 
 36  2c  nuclides of mass 36 (Mg,Al,Si,P,S,Cl,Ar,K,Ca) has been evaluated.  The 
 36  3c  principal sources of the 'adopted levels' presented for nuclides close 
 36  4c  to the stability line are Endt's evaluations (1990En08,1978En02).  The 
 36  4c  data sets for reactions and decays, including all available gamma-ray  
 36  6c  data, are based mostly on the original literature. The {+36}Na has     
 36  7c  been looked for but not yet experimentally detected.  There are no     
 36  8c  data available for the excited states in {+36}Al, and for {+36}Mg and  
 36  8c  {+36}Ca, only one excited state is known.                              
 36   c  CUT$Literature available up to December 31, 2011 has been consulted.   
 36   c  COMM$The statistical analysis of |g-ray data and deduced level schemes 
 36  2c  is carried out through computer codes available at NNDC, BNL website:  
 36  3c  www.nndc.bnl.gov. The direct feedings to excited states in |b{+-} and  
 36  4c  |e decays have generally been computed from I(|g+ce) intensity         
 36  5c  balances at each level; the associated log| {Ift} values are           
 36  6c  calculated using log| {Ift} code. All Q values have been adopted from  
 36  7c  2011AuZZ and compared with those in 2003Au03.  In cases where weighted 
 36  8c  averaging procedures have been used and the number of independent      
 36  9c  measurements is small (four or less), the assigned uncertainty is      
 36  Ac  generally the higher of the two values: the one given by the averaging 
 36  Bc  procedure and the lowest uncertainty quoted for a measurement in the   
 36  Cc  dataset.                                                               
 36   c  ACKN$Previous evaluations of Peter Endt and Cor van der Leun (1990En08 
 36  2c  (including update 1998En04), 1978En02 and 1973EnVA) provided an        
 36  3c  invaluable resource for the current work. The evaluators thank Chris   
 36  4c  Wrede (NSCL, MSU) for a careful review of this work and for many       
 36  5c  constructive comments.                                                 
 36   c  FUND$Work supported by the Office of Nuclear Physics, Office of        
 36  xc  Science of the DOE of the United States. At McMaster, partial funding  
 36  xc  was received from the NSERC of Canada.                                 
 36   C  CIT$NDS 113, 1 (2012)                                                  
